{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_4e0eced866fd4ae9b5dd8c7b","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: svemir-web-intelligence\ndescription: Search and investigate the public internet through Svemir's profile-aware multi-source infrastructure when a question benefits from current web evidence, source discovery, comparison, provenance, or an evolving sequence of queries. Use for quick lookups and deep web exploration; hand persistent programs to svemir-research when the search becomes a continuing body of work.\n---\n\n# Svemir Web Intelligence\n\nTreat web search as an adaptive sensing system, not a query box. Understand intent, choose complementary source profiles, preserve provenance, compare disagreement, and let useful results improve the next question.\n\n## Modes\n\n- **Direct:** one fact, page or quick verification. Use general web, answer briefly and cite the strongest direct source.\n- **Triangulated:** consequential or disputed question. Merge general and relevant specialist profiles; compare independent sources.\n- **Exploratory:** unclear vocabulary or new field. Search broadly, extract terms and actors, then issue narrower child queries.\n- **Forensic:** failures and implementation reality. Combine official material with code, issue trackers and technical communities; label testimony.\n\nDo not inflate a direct lookup into a research program. When work needs durable questions, claims, sessions and checkpoints, continue with `svemir-research` and retain this skill as its search organ.\n\n## Movement\n\n0. **Start from what earlier searches learned:** `node tools/pretraga.js ulaz \"<query>\"` prints the inferred profiles, which providers will run (and which a lesson marks dead), matching lessons from every project, provider health from the trace and similar past queries. This applies to CLI WebSearch/WebFetch too. When a source surprises you (dead, blocks the mask, 200 without content, derived, reliably good), record it in the same minute with `node tools/pretraga.js dodaj '<json>'`. The lessons live in `db/lekcije.jsonl` (spine, `merge=union`); `lib/search.js` skips a provider that a confirmed, fresh lesson marks dead and writes the consulted lesson ids into the trace.\n1. Express the real information need and what the answer could change.\n2. Select profiles: `general`, `site`, `reference`, `academic`, `biomedical`, `code`, `community`, `books`, `archive`, `data`.\n3. Vary query function, not only wording: orientation, primary evidence, implementation, failure, counterexample and recency.\n4. Search the smallest useful set first. Expand when uncertainty, disagreement or weak provenance remains.\n5. Open direct sources before making strong claims. Search snippets are discovery evidence only.\n6. Preserve provider and URL provenance. Distinguish primary evidence, synthesis, implementation and testimony.\n7. Keep failed queries, provider health and learned vocabulary outside the model prompt; retrieve only what the next decision needs.\n\n## Infrastructure invariants\n\n- General web intelligence is the base infrastructure; specialist engines are views through it.\n- Provider failure degrades locally through circuit breaking and failover, never globally.\n- Prefer structured, keyless public APIs. Respect rate limits and access controls.\n- Merge complementary sources for specialist or high-consequence questions; use cheap failover for ordinary lookups.\n- Agreement between engines raises discovery confidence, not truth confidence.\n- Raw telemetry is append-only evidence: complete, honest and inspectable. Compress only the model-facing view; never rewrite or discard the underlying trace.\n- Give models compact state, relevant evidence and exceptions by default, with direct drill-down into the raw trace for diagnosis and audit.\n- Never treat absence from results as proof of absence or novelty.\n\nUse `webSearch(query, options)` from `lib/search.js`. Read [references/provider-map.md](references/provider-map.md) when changing routing or diagnosing coverage.\n\nRead [references/evaluation.md](references/evaluation.md) when evaluating search quality or changing routing behavior. Keep the raw trace and derived score separate so a flattering summary cannot alter the evidence.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2249e90f-f5b3-4dba-94e3-6ed4eca44330","uuid":"d73f4591-cb13-4a34-bc3f-d8d16681149d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T21:43:26.416Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---\nname: svemir-web-intelligence\ndescription: Search and investigate the public internet through Svemir's profile-aware multi-source infrastructure when a question benefits from current web evidence, source discovery, comparison, provenance, or an evolving sequence of queries. Use for quick lookups and deep web exploration; hand persistent programs to svemir-research when the search becomes a continuing body of work.\n---\n\n# Svemir Web Intelligence\n\nTreat web search as an adaptive sensing system, not a query box. Understand intent, choose complementary source profiles, preserve provenance, compare disagreement, and let useful results improve the next question.\n\n## Modes\n\n- **Direct:** one fact, page or quick verification. Use general web, answer briefly and cite the strongest direct source.\n- **Triangulated:** consequential or disputed question. Merge general and relevant specialist profiles; compare independent sources.\n- **Exploratory:** unclear vocabulary or new field. Search broadly, extract terms and actors, then issue narrower child queries.\n- **Forensic:** failures and implementation reality. Combine official material with code, issue trackers and technical communities; label testimony.\n\nDo not inflate a direct lookup into a research program. When work needs durable questions, claims, sessions and checkpoints, continue with `svemir-research` and retain this skill as its search organ.\n\n## Movement\n\n0. **Start from what earlier searches lear