{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026102606004285e5a8b6d8694dc1","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"WebSearch denied again. So this restarted session runs without network permissions and without access to the base folder.\n\nGiven the constraint, the professional move:\n1. Tell the user plainly: the restarted session lost network grants + base-folder read access; web verification can't proceed until they re-grant (WebSearch/WebFetch/Bash-curl) and re-add the medijana_baza directory.\n2. Deliver what I can honestly NOW: `nalaz.md` + `prostorni_izvori.json` in gis_udaljena with:\n   - Section \"provereno u bazi (lokalno, sa diska)\" — from the base files I read earlier in this session (before the crash): OSM polygon 5.7 ha, coordinates, DEM estimates, geofizika, vodeni sloj URLs (the base records URLs like rai.ai.ac.rs Pop-Lazić PDF, DOI of Starinar LXI — those were recorded by earlier sessions with verification; I can cite them as *base-recorded* with their existing poverenje, marked \"zabeleženo u bazi, ovom sesijom nije ponovo otvoreno\").\n   - Section \"kandidati — NIJE provereno (nema mrežnih ovlašćenja)\" for each of the 5 areas, with candidate URLs and what to check. poverenje: \"nisko (neprovereno)\". dostupno_danas: \"nepoznato — proveriti kad mreža bude odobrena\".\n3. No fabrication of elevations: the DEM sampling task (Vlaško brdo kote) cannot be done — state that explicitly as an unfinished item.\n\nActually wait — before concluding, let me test whether Bash local commands still work and whether Write works (needed for deliverables). Test: `ls` in cwd (worked earlier), then Write a small test? I'll just write the real deliverable — if Write is denied, that's another blocker to report. Better: first quick `ls` test, then compose the files.\n\nLet me also reconsider: is there anything on disk in gis_udaljena besides ZADATAK.md and log? No (ls showed only those). The user's claim \"već skinuti izvori na disku\" — the base has pdf/ and osm/wd JSONs, which I read earlier (osm_nominatim.json, wd_q960839.json, osm_way_full.json exist; I didn't read their full content, only grep matches). I can't read them now. But from the earlier grep I got coordinates. The README summary gives OSM polygon ~5.7 ha.\n\nFor the DEM estimates (vila ~197–198 m, vodotoranj ~206 m) — that's in ZADATAK.md itself, fine.\n\nSo the deliverable structure is clear. Content per task area with candidates from my knowledge — each clearly labeled as unverified candidate with what to check. Candidate URLs I'm fairly confident about (to be marked as candidates, not verified):\n- Kanitz: Wikimedia Commons scans; archive.org search \"Römische Funde in Serbien\"; digi.ub.uni-heidelberg.de\n- mapire.eu (Habsburg military surveys) — Niš coverage uncertain (Niš was Ottoman until 1878; Third survey ended 1887 and covered Bosnia after 1878; Serbia south of border not covered — actually the Third Military Survey did NOT cover Serbia proper. But WWI occupation maps of Serbia (1915-1918, 1:75,000 and 1:200,000 Generalkarte) exist; ÖNB AKON digitized war maps.\n- Serbian: geosrbija.rs (RGZ), geoportal.rs, data.gov.rs, nasledje.gov.rs, fastionline.org, pleiades.stoa.org, DARE, AOR.\n- Copernicus: dataspace.copernicus.eu browser, GLO-30 on AWS/Azure/OpenTopography; SRTM on USGS EarthExplorer; ALOS AW3D30 (JAXA); MERIT DEM; EU-DEM (EEA, covers EEA39 incl. Serbia? v1.1 covers 39 countries — Serbia is EEA39 member? Serbia is a cooperating country of EEA — EU-DEM v1.1 coverage does include the West Balkans I believe; must verify).\n- Sentinel-2 via Copernicus Browser; Pleiades via Airbus (commercial); Google Earth Pro historical slider (desktop app free).\n- LiDAR Serbia: national LiDAR flight exists? Verify \"Airborne laser scanning Srbija RGZ\" — I recall RGZ ran LiDAR for some projects but no open national DTM; some city LiDAR projects. Must verify — will mark as open question with pointers.\n- NATO COBALT: unlikely public — mark as probably-not-public candidate with reasoning.\n\nAlso aerophotoarchaeology: known regional work — Institute of Archaeology Belgrade aerial prospection projects; Starinar 61/2011 geophysics paper (already in base) mentions future aerial prospection? The base geofizika layer says \"buduća prospekcija ka Nišavi\". Any cropmark analysis for Mediana — I know of none offhand; mark as \"nije nađeno u bazi; kandidat za pretragu\".\n\nOne more consideration: I could still do real verification via... no. No network path. OK.\n\nLet me also double-check Bash still works locally and Write permission, then write both files. To be efficient: one Bash `ls` test + then Write nalaz.md + Write prostorni_izvori.json in parallel? Write depends on knowing Write works — but if it fails I'll see and report. I'll do Bash test and both Writes in one go (they're independent; failure mode is visible per-call).\n\nActually — the JSON must be careful and honest. Let me draft the entries.\n\nprostorni_izvori.json entries (id, tip, rezolucija/godina, url, licenca, dostupno_danas, vrednost_za_3d, poverenje):\n\nGroup A — provereno kroz raniji rad baze (zapisi postoje, URL-ovi zabeleženi u bazi; ovom sesijom nisu ponovo otvoreni):\n1. osm-poligon-jezgra: OSM way (osm_way_full.json lokalno), ~5,7 ha, ODbL, dostupno (API overpass/osm) — vrednost: osnova situacije; poverenje: visoko za poligon (preuzet), srednje za identifikaciju sa vilom.\n2. wikidata-q960839: Mediana Wikidata item, CC0, coordinates 43.31028, 21.94889.\n3. pop-lazic-2018 PDF: https://rai.ai.ac.rs/bitstream/id/2194/ROMAN_LIMES_AND_CITIES_ON_THE_TERRITORY.pdf — open access, vodeni sloj primarni izvor.\n4. starinar-61-2011 geofizika DOI 10.2298/STA1161275M — DOI/naucni izvor, open access at doiserbia.nb.rs (kandidat URL — markirati).\n\nHmm — careful: doiserbia URL is a candidate. I'll mark clearly which URLs are \"u bazi zabeležen/otvoren ranije\" vs \"kandidat, nije otvoren\".\n\nActually the cleanest honest split: `status_provere`: \"otvoreno_u_bazi_ranije\" | \"neprovereno (ova sesija bez mreže)\". The schema asked is fixed: {id, tip, rezolucija/godina, url, licenca, dostupno_danas, vrednost_za_3d, poverenje}. I can add `status_provere` as extra field — schema says \"niz: {...}\" with those keys; adding one extra key is reasonable and increases honesty. I'll add it.\n\nGroup B — kandidati (neprovereno):\n5. kanitz-1892-römische-funde: archive.org search URL; value: prvi planovi Medijane 19. veka; dostupno: nepoznato.\n6. kanitz-serbien-1868: archive.org.\n7. wikimedia-kanitz-medijana: commons category search.\n8. mapire-habsburg: https://mapire.eu — third military survey; caveat Niš van habzburškog obuhvata do 1918.\n9. onb-akon: http://data.onb.ac.at/akon — WWI karte Srbije.\n10. mapster-amzp: http://mapy.amzp.pl — nemačke/austro karte istočne Evrope (WIG, Generalkarte 1:200k list Niš).\n11. rgz-aerofoto: https://www.geosrbija.rs / geoportal.rs — aerofoto snimci, DTM; dostupnost neizvesna.\n12. usgs-earthexplorer-declassified: https://earthexplorer.usgs.gov — SRTM + declassified; CORONA pokrivenost Jugoslavije neizvesna.\n13. nato-cobalt-1999: verovatno nejavno; kandidat za proveru (izveštaji, ne podaci).\n14. sentinel-2 copernicus browser: https://browser.dataspace.copernicus.eu — 10 m, free, otvoreno (visoko poverenje da postoji usluga; Niš pokrivenost — svaka kopnena površina; to je sigurno. Ali \"otvoreno_mis_proverom\" ne mogu tvrditi — jezično: usluga javno poznata; provera u ovoj sesiji nije izvršena).\n15. pleiades-airbus: https://www.intelligence-airbusds.com — komercijalno 50 cm.\n16. google-earth-historical: desktop Pro free; istorijski slajder za Niš (pozna funkcija).\n17. copernicus-glo30: https://spacedata.copernicus.eu / AWS — 30 m, otvoren. Za DEM proveru ključno.\n18. srtm-30m: earthexplorer — postojeći izvor baze.\n19. aw3d30-jaxa: https://www.eorc.jaxa.jp/ALOS/en/aw3d30/ — 30 m free.\n20. eu-dem: https://land.copernicus.eu/imagery-in-situ/eu-dem — v1.1 obuhvat EEA39 (Srbija?) — pitanje za proveru.\n21. opentopodata-api: https://www.opentopodata.org — besplatan API sa eu-dem i srtm skupovima — alat za kote, ne izvor podataka.\n22. nasledje-gov-rs: http://nasledje.gov.rs — registar nepokretnih dobara (Medijana = spomenik kulture od izuzetnog značaja); predmet \"AN 22\" tražiti.\n23. geoportal-rgz-inspire: https://geoportal.rgz.gov.rs — INSPIRE usluge Srbije.\n24. fasti-online: http://www.fastionline.org — zapisi iskopa; Medijana?\n25. pleiades-naissus: https://pleiades.stoa.org — Naissus/Mediana zapisi.\n26. aerofotoarheologija: kandidati za literaturu (aerial archaeology Serbia projects) — bez URL-a pouzdanog; označiti kao istraživačko pitanje.\n\nThat's a lot of entries; fine.\n\nBut hold on — I want to avoid over-filling with unverified candidates presented as findings. The nalaz.md must be crystal clear: deliverable is ~80% \"puni spisak kandidata sa planom provere\", plus \"šta je stvarno provereno\" (lokalni podaci baze). And explicit blocker section. Also: I should NOT sample elevations — mark as nedovršeno.\n\nAlternative approach: should I ask the user for permissions and stop? The user explicitly said \"na kraju predaj nalaz.md\" — they want the deliverable this turn. I'll produce it with honest flags AND clearly tell them what to re-enable for the verification pass. That's the best of both.\n\nLet me test Bash + Write now.","signature":"9bfd280787964402829ed71a"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2249e90f-f5b3-4dba-94e3-6ed4eca44330","uuid":"a9cd8c19-2536-4047-8467-821317e50124","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:01:47.670Z"}
